# Coach speech (Hindi): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
#
# Always positive, never blaming. The coach says "तुम". The player's gender is unknown, and a Hindi verb agrees
# with its subject: never "तुम जीत गए", "तुम जीत रहे थे", "देखते रहो" (the participle agrees too). Instead:
# transitive perfectives with ने, which agree with the object ("तुमने बाज़ी जीत ली", "तुमने मुझे हरा दिया"),
# dative subjects ("तुम्हें बेहतर चाल मिली"), nouns ("तुम्हारी जीत"), "बाज़ी तुम्हारे हाथ में थी" for "you were
# winning", the passive, and "... जारी रखो" for "keep doing".
# A verb never agrees with a counted noun ("1 ग़लती हुई" / "3 ग़लतियाँ हुईं"): counts stand in nominal phrases,
# after a colon, or as an object with को ("तुमने {n:piece_obl} को काटा").
# Forms from common.lang: "{n:moveno}" = a move number ("चाल 21" written, "इक्कीसवीं चाल" spoken: "{n:moveno} पर" =
# "at move 21", "{crit_no:moveno} तक" = "until move 21"); "{acc:percent}" = "85%" (spoken "पचासी प्रतिशत");
# "{moves:move_obl} में" = "in 30 moves"; "{pts:point_obl} का फ़ायदा" = "a gain of 3 points";
# "{n:best_move}" = "5 सबसे अच्छी चालें".
# Moves ({move}, {crit_move}, {crit_best}), {eval} and {opening} are quoted names: after a colon, or before a comma,
# never before a postposition, a copula or a verb.
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level}:
#   appraisal.phase.*   bare nouns (ओपनिंग is feminine, मिडिलगेम and एंडगेम masculine): the lines never make a
#                       verb or adjective agree with them; "{text} में" is fine (they do not change before a
#                       postposition).
#   appraisal.reason.*  an adverbial phrase said after "ड्रॉ, " ("ड्रॉ, आपसी सहमति से।").
#   theme.*             an infinitive (-ना) or noun phrase, said after a colon; "अपना" for the player's own pieces (the
#                       player is the doer of the infinitive).
#   appraisal.level.*   the coach level names of the menus (coach.level.N.name), quoted “...” by the lines and
#                       followed by "स्तर" where the sentence needs a noun.

